{"id": "sdqa0007", "pool": "sdqa", "arm": "balanced", "tier": "balanced", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 3097460736, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "f4bb2b6e6cb68bd1527d1ee0e21321345a1bb395842da8101a511dc9dc7ef77e", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.7972545623779297, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 7, "query": "What's the difference between man-slaughter and homicide?", "input_path": "/data/sdqa_audio/sdqa0007.wav", "input_sha256": "b5dc29ee8e124e827cfdaf5e731d518c51f4ff1928c7f96aa9100fdf5acb4cf2", "input_samples": 101370, "input_s": 6.336, "n_real_chunks": 7, "score": 0.2929, "act": 0.999, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Manslaughter and homicide are both crimes involving the killing of a person, but they differ in intent and circumstances. Homic ide typically involves the unlawful killing of another with intent to kill or while committing a serious crime like rape or murder. Man slaughter is usually less severe and can result from actions that are reckless or negligent rather than intentional. For example, vi olent acts committed during the heat of passion might be considered manslaughter because the killer didn' t plan to kill but acted impuls ively. So, ho mic ide implies intent, while manslaughter suggests a lack of it due to reck lessness or diminished responsibility.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 6, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 36, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sdqa/audio/sdqa0007_balanced_local.wav", "sha256": "5e4de6fef17ccde889fd8b0c5ddeffeb198c52e1605dd4e047b34395f78a7779", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 36.16